{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "ash-6",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "probe",
      "reason": "The existing probe interface already supports investigating nearby subjects and physically testing small owned material samples without eating them. This matches an evidence-limited investigation, rather than a guarantee of food safety. Observing plant stock and growth does not establish nutrition, toxicity or preparation requirements. Unsupported properties must remain unknown; neither the food's name nor an unsuccessful test establishes safety.",
      "specification": "Reuse probe's current executable contract and sample-test schema, not a new assay or food-processing capability. Observation requires actual local access; destructive material testing requires an actual owned sample, consumes 0.1 material unit and costs 0.5 energy over one round. Observation costs 0.2 energy over one round. The nearby plant's stock is not an owned sample, and review supplies none. Preserve sample identity, origin, age, test conditions, measured results and unresolved questions in personal records. Report nutrition, toxicity or preparation effects only where the implemented test actually measures them; distinguish an undetected hazard from evidence of absence. Do not expose underlying food parameters as experimental findings merely because they exist in world state. No consumption, detoxification, prepared food or safety certification is implied. Use existing shared reference, reach, ownership, completion and cancellation rules; an interrupted trial must not duplicate or erase material. Any subsequently needed analytical or processing mechanism not implemented by probe requires its own concrete development handoff, not a fabricated probe result.",
      "experienceReview": "A successful experiment establishing genuinely new information may use the existing grounded-understanding source: probe emits information-confirmed with qualified=true for the actual investigator, supported by the recorded test. Its transient amount is 0.8, cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition and 12-round cooldown. Its maintained component gains 0.035 on qualifying events and decays 0.0015 under the registered bounded maintenance rule. Already known facts, inconclusive trials, requesting and learning do not qualify. Do not add a duplicate source. Testing alone provides no nutrition, healing or physical comfort.",
      "visualReview": "Use probe's existing trial-result, trial-material-consumed and information-confirmed event bindings. Show the actual subject or sample, paid material loss, performed test, observed result and explicitly unknown properties in the event log and retained evidence view. Replay must distinguish observation from destructive testing and must not display a safe-food badge or preparation-success effect without supporting results. No new object, collision geometry or visual effect with physical consequences is introduced.",
      "learning": 0
    }
  ]
}
